<p><strong>Depth 1 — lens on <em>L2-19: HTTP request smuggling (awareness for architects)</em>:</strong> When logs “mysteriously stop,” think <strong>time sync failure</strong>, collector saturation, retention misconfiguration, or attacker tampering—in that diagnostic order for a fair exam narrative.</p>
